// One charge (0.5 kg) on the floor of a 0.75 m tunnel through soft rock (sandstone, `r`; limestone breaks
// the same): it blows a crater through the 1 m floor to the bedrock and 1.25 m up into the roof, broken in patches out to 2.5 m along the
// tunnel, and leaves the rock 3.5 m off whole. About 155 tiles of rock are broken, and the rubble is thrown
// metres along the tunnel.
